exports[`ds --json > add, react: writes the registry item and its dependencies, then changes nothing on a second run 1`] = `
{
  "apiVersion": 1,
  "data": {
    "dependencies": [
      "@fontsource-variable/inter@^5.3.0",
      "@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans-arabic@^5.3.0",
      "radix-ui@^1.8.1",
    ],
    "framework": "react",
    "imports": [
      "import './components/ds/ds.css';  // once, at the app root",
      "import './components/ds/style-studio.css';  // or another style",
      "import { Theme } from './components/ds/react/theme';",
      "import { Kbd } from './components/ds/react/components/Kbd';",
    ],
    "install": "npm install @fontsource-variable/inter@^5.3.0 @fontsource/ibm-plex-sans-arabic@^5.3.0",
    "items": [
      "kbd",
      "core",
      "theme",
      "style-studio",
    ],
    "name": "Kbd",
    "shadcn": "npx shadcn@4.23.0 add @ds/kbd",
  },
  "type": "add.result",
}
`;

exports[`ds --json > docs 1`] = `
{
  "apiVersion": 1,
  "data": {
    "a11y": {
      "announce": "The spoken key names, or label. Nothing when decorative.",
      "focus": "Never focusable.",
      "keys": {},
      "native": {
        "accessibilityRole": "text",
      },
      "notes": [
        "The root is dir ltr and isolated (unicode-bidi isolate), so a shortcut reads Ctrl then K inside an Arabic sentence and does not move the punctuation around it.",
        "Menu items and buttons that have a shortcut set aria-keyshortcuts (ariaKeyShortcuts from the same helpers) and render Kbd decorative.",
        "No hover, press or motion: a keycap is text, not a control.",
        "Under forced colors the gradient and the depth shadow drop; each key keeps a CanvasText border.",
        "The default spoken names are English and carry lang en, so an Arabic page reads them with an English voice. Pass label for names in another language.",
      ],
      "role": "None: a kbd element. Each keycap is hidden; a visually hidden span (spoken) says the key names, so a screen reader hears Control Shift P, not C T R L plus.",
    },
    "anatomy": [
      "root",
      "key",
      "separator",
      "spoken",
    ],
    "avoidWhen": [
      "Code, a file name or a command people type, which is not a key press",
      "A label on a button people click",
      "The only way to learn an action: a shortcut is an extra path, the action needs a visible control too",
    ],
    "content": {
      "ar": {
        "digits": "Western digits.",
        "keys": "Keys stay in Latin letters and read left to right: Ctrl+K, never translated or mirrored.",
        "sentence": "اضغط Ctrl+K للبحث. The key names are spoken in English by default; pass label for another wording.",
      },
      "en": {
        "keys": "Key names as printed on keyboards: Ctrl, Shift, Alt, Esc, Enter, Tab, single letters in upper case.",
        "sentence": "Put the shortcut after the verb: Press Ctrl+K to open search.",
      },
    },
    "family": "data-display",
    "frameworks": {
      "angular": {
        "behavior": "kbd[dsKbd], hand built on shortcut.ts",
        "status": "planned",
      },
      "native": {
        "note": "Touch first apps rarely show shortcuts; useful on iPad and Android with a hardware keyboard. Same shortcut.ts.",
        "status": "planned",
      },
      "react": {
        "behavior": "hand built kbd elements",
        "example": "Kbd.demo.tsx",
        "note": "Parsing, the Mod mapping and spoken names live in @the-system/shared (shortcut.ts), so Angular and native read the same keys.",
        "status": "ready",
      },
    },
    "insteadUse": {
      "A hint that explains a control": "Tooltip, with Kbd in its shortcut part",
      "A removable value or a filter": "Chip",
      "A status or a count next to a label": "Badge",
      "Code or a command people type": "Code (wave 2), or a monospace text span",
    },
    "kind": "component",
    "markdown": "# Kbd

A key or a keyboard shortcut drawn as keycaps, with the key names spoken to screen readers.

## Use when

- Telling people which key or shortcut runs an action: Ctrl+K opens search
- The shortcut part of a menu item, a tooltip or a command palette row
- A keyboard help sheet that lists shortcuts next to what they do

## Do not use when

- Code, a file name or a command people type, which is not a key press
- A label on a button people click
- The only way to learn an action: a shortcut is an extra path, the action needs a visible control too

## Use instead

- Code or a command people type: Code (wave 2), or a monospace text span
- A status or a count next to a label: Badge
- A removable value or a filter: Chip
- A hint that explains a control: Tooltip, with Kbd in its shortcut part

## Anatomy

\`root\`, \`key\`, \`separator\`, \`spoken\`

## Accessibility

- Role: None: a kbd element. Each keycap is hidden; a visually hidden span (spoken) says the key names, so a screen reader hears Control Shift P, not C T R L plus.
- Focus: Never focusable.
- Announce: The spoken key names, or label. Nothing when decorative.

## Common mistakes

- Wrong: <kbd>Ctrl+Shift+P</kbd> as one cap, read as C T R L plus
  Right: Kbd with the shortcut string: three keycaps and the spoken names
- Wrong: Hard coding ⌘ for everyone
  Right: Mod+K, which draws ⌘K on a Mac and Ctrl+K elsewhere
- Wrong: A shortcut in an Arabic sentence that renders K+Ctrl
  Right: Kbd, which keeps the keys left to right inside right to left text
- Wrong: A menu item whose shortcut is read twice
  Right: aria-keyshortcuts on the item and Kbd decorative

## Frameworks

- react: ready (example Kbd.demo.tsx)
- angular: planned
- native: planned
",
    "mistakes": [
      {
        "right": "Kbd with the shortcut string: three keycaps and the spoken names",
        "wrong": "<kbd>Ctrl+Shift+P</kbd> as one cap, read as C T R L plus",
      },
      {
        "right": "Mod+K, which draws ⌘K on a Mac and Ctrl+K elsewhere",
        "wrong": "Hard coding ⌘ for everyone",
      },
      {
        "right": "Kbd, which keeps the keys left to right inside right to left text",
        "wrong": "A shortcut in an Arabic sentence that renders K+Ctrl",
      },
      {
        "right": "aria-keyshortcuts on the item and Kbd decorative",
        "wrong": "A menu item whose shortcut is read twice",
      },
    ],
    "name": "Kbd",
    "slug": "kbd",
    "summary": "A key or a keyboard shortcut drawn as keycaps, with the key names spoken to screen readers.",
    "useWhen": [
      "Telling people which key or shortcut runs an action: Ctrl+K opens search",
      "The shortcut part of a menu item, a tooltip or a command palette row",
      "A keyboard help sheet that lists shortcuts next to what they do",
    ],
  },
  "type": "docs.page",
}
`;

